{#
    A table, addressed rather than drawn.

    What a document writes is the table's own children — the caption, the
    column widths a `:widths:` option worked out, the head and the body, cells
    and all, because a cell carries a link or a literal and no property could.
    The `<table>` itself, its density and the box it scrolls in are the
    element's, which is what keeps a page of this theme and a page of a product
    the same table.

    Always scrollable: `sds-table` gives a table the column, and one whose
    own minimum is wider than that has to go somewhere. The box is around the
    table and never the table itself — `overflow-x` on a `<table>` needs
    `display: block`, which leaves table layout and shrink-wraps every table
    that was not too wide in the first place.

    What is not carried over is the core's own class list — `colwidths-auto`,
    `align-*`, `grid-*`. No stylesheet here defines them, so they drew nothing
    before and name nothing now.
#}
<sds-table scrollable
    {%- if tableNode.hasOption('width') %} width="{{ tableNode.option('width') }}"{% endif %}>
    {%- include "body/table/table-caption.html.twig" -%}
    {%- include "body/table/table-colgroups.html.twig" -%}
    {%- include "body/table/table-header.html.twig" -%}
    {%- include "body/table/table-body.html.twig" -%}
</sds-table>
